        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Colonial rule</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1415 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Power held by</span><span class="info-stat-val">A distant metropolitan state, crown or chartered company, acting through appointed governors, viceroys and officials, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a> through local rulers it supervised</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Legitimacy from</span><span class="info-stat-val">Conquest, treaties made under pressure, papal grants and claims of discovery, justified by a Christian or “civilising” mission and by beliefs in racial superiority</span></div>
